---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { AFFILIATE_LINKS_ACTIVE } from '../data/providers';
---

<Base
  title="How Company Name Checker is funded"
  description="Company Name Checker is free and independent. How the site is funded, whether any links earn us money, and how we keep comparisons fair."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "How we're funded", href: '/disclosure/' }]}
>
  <h1>How we're funded</h1>
  <p class="lede">Company Name Checker is free to use, and it stays independent of Companies House and of every provider we mention.</p>

  {
    AFFILIATE_LINKS_ACTIVE ? (
      <>
        <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
        <p>
          Some links to providers, such as company registration services and business accounts, are affiliate links: if
          you sign up through them, we may receive a commission. This doesn't change the price you pay.
        </p>
        <p>Affiliate links are labelled where they appear.</p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <h2>We don't earn from any links yet</h2>
        <p>
          No provider pays us, and none of the links on this site earn us a commission. We link to Tide, ANNA, banks
          and Companies House because they're useful to people setting up a company, not because we're paid to.
        </p>
        <p>
          In future we may join affiliate programmes, for example with company registration or business account
          providers. If we do, we'll update this page and label every affiliate link where it appears. It won't change
          the price you pay.
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }

  <h2>How we keep comparisons fair</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every comparison includes options that don't pay us, including registering directly with Companies House.</li>
    <li>
      Prices and terms come from each provider's own published pages, with a link and the date we checked them. See
      <a href="/sources/">sources</a> and <a href="/data-updates/">data updates</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Whether a provider pays us never decides whether it appears or where it's listed.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
